<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Age</h1>
<p>Your character grows older all the time, online or not: one year of game 
time passes in about 42 real hours. Your age and race are shown by 
<a cmd='#'>score</a>. Every character is born with a lifespan, which depends on the 
race: a human lives some 80 to 110 years, a dwarf about 400, an elf over 
a thousand.
</p><p>Age changes your body. Young characters have more endurance than anyone: 
it peaks early in life and then falls slowly, down to a fifth at the end 
of your lifespan. Mana works the other way: it grows with age, and the 
old have the most. Hit points don't change with age.
</p><p>When you outlive your lifespan, your body gives out: your maximum hit 
points, mana and endurance drop to almost nothing. If you log in in that 
state, Odin revives you, two years short of the end. To win back more 
years, seek the Eternal Spring, close to the Top of the Hill in the 
Cypress Forest: drinking from it (drink twice to be sure) makes you ten 
years younger, though never younger than a fifth of your lifespan.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
